/*
  ESP32-CAM Robot - corrected for the uploaded schematic

  Hardware used by this code (TB6612FNG / SparkFun ROB-14450):
    GPIO12 -> PWMA and PWMB (tied together in the schematic)
    GPIO2  -> AIN1
    GPIO13 -> AIN2
    GPIO15 -> BIN1
    GPIO14 -> BIN2
    STBY   -> +5V (hard-wired enabled)
    GPIO4  -> LED

  Because PWMA and PWMB share GPIO12, the firmware holds that common enable
  high and applies PWM to the direction inputs. This keeps independent speed
  control for Motor A and Motor B without changing the PCB. Motor A/J6 is
  treated as left and Motor B/J7 as right.

  Motor experimentation controls:
    - Independent left and right motor sliders.
    - Full PWM range: 0-255 for each motor.
    - Optional motor sync checkbox.
    - Exact -1 / +1 PWM adjustment buttons.
    - Sliders update the motors live while driving.
    - Short 255 PWM kick when a motor starts from zero.

  Network fallback:
    - Try configured Wi-Fi for 10 seconds.
    - If unavailable, start ESP32-Robot-XXXX access point.
    - Fallback AP password: 88888888
    - Fallback page: http://192.168.4.1
    - AP remains available while STA periodically retries normal Wi-Fi.

  Browser OTA:
    - OTA password: 88888888
    - Upload an exported Arduino .bin from the debug sidebar.
    - Motors are stopped before writing firmware.
    - Requires an OTA-capable partition scheme flashed once by USB.

  USB/UART0 serial console:
    - 115200 baud, 8N1.
    - ESP32 U0T / GPIO1 -> USB-TTL RX.
    - ESP32 U0R / GPIO3 <- USB-TTL TX.
    - Common GND. Use 3.3V TTL signalling, not RS-232 voltage levels.
    - Commands: help, status, log, camera, stop.

  Camera settings sidebar:
    - Resolution, display rotation (0/90/180/270), JPEG quality,
      brightness, contrast, saturation, vertical flip, horizontal mirror,
      and reset-to-defaults.
    - 90/270 rotation is browser-side to avoid expensive JPEG re-encoding.
*/

